📘 API Documentation

Base URL:
http://localhost:5000/api

All endpoints return JSON responses.
Use Content-Type: application/json when sending data.

👤 1. Citizens API
Table: citizens
Column	Type	Description
id	SERIAL	Primary key
nin	VARCHAR(20)	National ID Number
last_name_ar	VARCHAR(100)	Last name (Arabic)
first_name_ar	VARCHAR(100)	First name (Arabic)
last_name_lat	VARCHAR(100)	Last name (Latin)
first_name_lat	VARCHAR(100)	First name (Latin)
wilaya	VARCHAR(100)	Wilaya name
municipality	VARCHAR(100)	Municipality name
created_at	TIMESTAMP	Auto timestamp
🟢 GET /api/citizens

Description: Fetch all citizens
Response Example:

[
  {
    "id": 1,
    "nin": "1234567890",
    "last_name_ar": "بن عمر",
    "first_name_ar": "سارة",
    "last_name_lat": "Benomar",
    "first_name_lat": "Sara",
    "wilaya": "Guelma",
    "municipality": "Oued Zenati",
    "created_at": "2025-10-19T13:24:07.472Z"
  }
]

🟢 GET /api/citizens/:id

Description: Fetch one citizen by ID
Example: /api/citizens/1

🟡 POST /api/citizens

Description: Create new citizen
Request Example:

{
  "nin": "1234567890",
  "lastname_ar": "بن عمر",
  "firstname_ar": "سارة",
  "lastname_lat": "Benomar",
  "firstname_lat": "Sara",
  "wilaya": "Guelma",
  "municipality": "Oued Zenati"
}

🔵 PUT /api/citizens/:id

Description: Update existing citizen
Request Example:

{
  "nin": "1234567890",
  "lastname_ar": "بن عمر",
  "firstname_ar": "سارة",
  "lastname_lat": "Benomar",
  "firstname_lat": "Sara",
  "wilaya": "Guelma",
  "municipality": "Oued Zenati"
}

🔴 DELETE /api/citizens/:id

Description: Delete a citizen by ID

📋 2. Control Lists API
Table: control_lists
Column	Type	Description
control_list_id	SERIAL	Primary key
name	VARCHAR(100)	Control list name
description	TEXT	Description
created_by	INT	FK → users(user_id)
created_at	TIMESTAMP	Auto timestamp
🟢 GET /api/control-lists

Description: Get all control lists
Response Example:

[
  {
    "control_list_id": 1,
    "name": "Vehicle Safety Check",
    "description": "List for checking vehicles' safety and documents",
    "created_by": 1,
    "created_at": "2025-10-19T14:00:00.000Z"
  }
]

🟢 GET /api/control-lists/:id

Description: Get one control list by ID

🟡 POST /api/control-lists

Description: Create a control list
Request Example:

{
  "name": "Vehicle Inspection",
  "description": "Checklist for road safety",
  "created_by": 1
}

🔵 PUT /api/control-lists/:id

Description: Update control list
Request Example:

{
  "name": "Updated Vehicle Inspection",
  "description": "Updated checklist with new safety rules"
}

🔴 DELETE /api/control-lists/:id

Description: Delete control list

🚓 3. Controls API

Represents each inspection or control operation, linking a citizen to a control list.

Table: controls
Column	Type	Description
control_id	SERIAL	Primary key
citizen_id	INT	FK → citizens(id)
control_list_id	INT	FK → control_lists(control_list_id)
controlled_by	INT	FK → users(user_id)
notes	TEXT	Optional
created_at	TIMESTAMP	Auto timestamp
🟢 GET /api/controls

Description: Fetch all control records
Response Example:

[
  {
    "control_id": 1,
    "citizen_id": 22,
    "control_list_id": 3,
    "controlled_by": 5,
    "notes": "Citizen vehicle documents verified",
    "created_at": "2025-10-19T14:15:00.000Z"
  }
]

🟢 GET /api/controls/:id

Description: Fetch control by ID

🟡 POST /api/controls

Description: Create new control
Request Example:

{
  "citizen_id": 22,
  "control_list_id": 3,
  "controlled_by": 5,
  "notes": "Vehicle passed inspection"
}

🔵 PUT /api/controls/:id

Description: Update control record
Request Example:

{
  "notes": "Documents updated and verified"
}

🔴 DELETE /api/controls/:id

Description: Delete control record

⚠️ Response Status Codes
Code	Meaning
200	OK
201	Created
400	Bad Request
404	Not Found
500	Internal Server Error




add user api

Method: POST

URL: http://localhost:5000/api/users

Headers:

Content-Type: application/json


Body (raw JSON):

{
  "username": "john_doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "secret123",
  "groupId": 1
}

